00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.990 align:start position:0%
we aim to provide maximum information to  the public about our recycling scheme to  make it easy and convenient for our  customers to recycle as much of their  waste as possible  we deliver an ongoing programme of waste  education to engage local schools and  communities in the reduction of waste we  carry our collections of waste and  recycling from over 56,000 households in  team bridge and our vehicles go out  every weekday morning collecting  recycling and black bin waste all dry  recyclables are sorted onto the curbside  vehicles by our crews and delivered to  our Newton Abbot bulking station to be  segregated and transported to  reprocessing facilities all of the  material from Green wheelie bins gets  taken to a large composting facility and  the black bin waste goes to a nearby  landfill site we send out five  mechanical sweeper vehicles in the early  mornings to clean up the main town  centres and our parish sweepers go out  to rural towns and villages to keep the  streets clean and empty litter bins a  separate team the sponsor fly-tipping  incidents picking up waste has been  dumped in public areas there were 39  public toilets across team bridge and we  are responsible for their cleaning and  maintenance our toilets are assessed  annually for cleanliness and general  standard in recent years we've won  numerous loo of the Year awards with  many achieving a five-star grading we  continue to strive for maximum recycling  a minimum waste in team bridge and aim  to maintain our top ten position in the  national chance for recycling  performance and waste reduction
 

